    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (74.93) and **Christian Yelich** (74.33) pacing the offense, both representing the highest efficiency ceiling in the lineup. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start against Martin despite a moderate xERA, as his elite xwOBA of 0.478 provides a floor that few others can match. **Christian Yelich** benefits significantly from the matchup against Sugano; the combination of a favorable platoon advantage and his spot at the top of the order creates a premium environment for Runs and RBI generation. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (60.11) faces a stiffer test against Jones, his inclusion remains mandatory for the Zebras due to our organizational priority on stolen base efficiency; even with a slight negative adjustment for Jones's elite catcher, his sprint speed remains our most vital asset in a close Roto race.\n\nMid-tier value is anchored today by **Caleb Durbin** (67.91) and **Lars Nootbaar** (65.90), both of whom exploit favorable SP xERAs to maintain strong efficiency ratings. **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) also presents an intriguing profile; while his base projection is modest, the combination of a wind-aided park factor and a favorable matchup against a struggling Rodriguez (+19% SP skill adjustment) makes him a high-leverage play. On the bench, **Carson Benge** (51.93) was the most difficult exclusion. He showed strong indicators, but ultimately, the density of the middle-order performance from players like **Junior Caminero** (63.38) and the lineup security afforded to **Colt Keith** (59.78) pushed **Carson Benge** into a reserve role. \n\nRisk management remains a priority heading into the first pitch. We are monitoring a 41% rain risk surrounding **Lars Nootbaar**\u2019s matchup against Lowder, which could result in a shortened outing or a mid-game delay. Additionally, **Dillon Dingler** (41.89) is skating close to the Zebras' 40.0 efficiency floor; while he remains in the lineup due to his order placement, his negative platoon adjustment against Way suggests he is a candidate to be pulled early if the game script turns against him. We continue to keep **Hyeseong Kim** stashed while he remains in the minors, awaiting a roster spot opening.",
